INT. SALT MINE HANDBALL COURT - NIGHT

A court hacked out of rock salt, four hundred feet underground. The walls glitter pink under caged work lights. Every bounce of the ball leaves a puff of white dust.

DESTA ABEBE, 30s, lean, forearms taped to the elbow, bounces the ball once and catches it. Across the court stands "TINY" OKORO, 40s, six-foot-five and wide as a door, breathing through his mouth.

Score chalked on the wall: 14-14.

DESTA
Serve's mine, Tiny.

TINY
Serve's been yours for an hour.

Desta serves. A cracking low shot. Tiny lunges, returns it. Desta scrambles, returns it back. Dust rolls off the walls.

They trade six shots, each harder than the last. Tiny's sneaker slides on the salt. He recovers.

TINY (CONT'D)
You're hitting it flat, Desta.

DESTA
You're standing too deep.

TINY
Wanna tell me where to stand?

DESTA
Anywhere I'm not hitting.

The ball dies in the corner. Desta slaps the wall.

DESTA (CONT'D)
Mine.

TINY
Floor's wet. Your shoe slipped.

DESTA
My shoe didn't slip.

Tiny walks to the line, wipes his face with his shirt. The shirt comes away gray with salt.

TINY
Replay it, then.

DESTA
No replay.

TINY
The foreman said no replays, Desta. The foreman's gone home.

Beat. Desta picks the ball up off the floor and holds it out. Tiny doesn't take it.

TINY (CONT'D)
Fifteen. Next point wins, no more talk.

DESTA
You started the talking.

Tiny takes the ball. He bounces it once. A loose pebble of salt skitters across the floor.

TINY
Ready?

DESTA
Serve it, Tiny.

Tiny serves. The ball screams off the wall.

CUT TO BLACK.
